    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d871">

                <pb facs="0788" n="781" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg781"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.93/403a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Second Secretary of
                        Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at Nanking</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-09T17:00:00-05:00">December 9, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>372. Your 1021, December 9, 10 a.m<anchor n="93" xml:id="d871-f1"/> You will of
                    course keep in mind and be guided by the statement made in the Department’s 368,
                    November 30, 2 p.m., to the effect that you and staff should not expose
                    yourselves to imminent and serious danger.<anchor n="94" xml:id="d871-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
